            `The comparison below is factual and as balanced as the evidence allows. Where the Manmohan Singh government had genuine strategic justifications for its choices, those are presented. Where the BJP government has genuine achievements, those are presented. Where either government has genuine failures, those are presented.`,
            `<table><thead><tr><th><strong>Dimension</strong></th><th><strong>UPA (2004-2014): Manmohan Singh</strong></th><th><strong>BJP (2014-Present): Modi</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Response to 26/11 Mumbai (2008)</td><td>No military retaliation. Diplomatic isolation of Pakistan: UNSC sanctions on LeT, Hafiz Saeed on US bounty list, David Headley convicted in 2013. Home Minister resigned. NSA offered resignation. Strategic argument: correctly identified Pakistan Army's trap and refused to enable their FATA extraction</td><td>Not in power during 26/11. Inherited the aftermath. Article 370 abrogation in 2019 dismantled the political infrastructure that had provided local support for Pakistani-sponsored terrorism in Kashmir. Muridke facility that trained 26/11 attackers finally struck in 2025 under Operation Sindoor</td></tr><tr><td>Response to Uri (2016)</td><td>Not in power</td><td>Surgical strikes 11 days after attack. Para SF crossed LoC and struck launch pads inside PoK. First public acknowledgment in Indian history of crossing LoC. PM personally oversaw planning and gave go-ahead after military briefing. Changed deterrence calculus permanently</td></tr><tr><td>Response to Pulwama (2019)</td><td>Not in power</td><td>Balakot airstrikes 12 days after attack. IAF crossed International Boundary into undisputed Pakistan for first time since 1971. Struck JeM training facility in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa. Wing Commander Abhinandan captured and returned. Established India's willingness to escalate beyond LoC</td></tr><tr><td>Response to Pahalgam (2025)</td><td>Not in power</td><td>Operation Sindoor 15 days after attack. Nine targets struck across Pakistan and PoK including Muridke and Bahawalpur. All weapons fired from Indian airspace. 22-minute operation. Over 100 terrorists killed per government briefing. Pakistan's air defense bypassed and jammed</td></tr><tr><td>Defence procurement</td><td>Procurement paralysis: Rafale deal stalled for nearly a decade amid political controversy. AgustaWestland VVIP helicopter scam. Tenders cancelled and reissued repeatedly. Major modernisation programmes stalled. Critics called it a decade of equipping soldiers with obsolete hardware</td><td>Rafale jets finalised 2016, inducted 2020. S-400 procured despite US CAATSA pressure. BrahMos supersonic cruise missiles deployed. SiG 716 rifles for infantry. Apache attack helicopters. Chinook heavy lift. CDS created 2020. LEMOA, COMCASA, BECA signed 2016-2020. Defence exports from Rs 1,500 crore to Rs 21,000 crore</td></tr><tr><td>Terrorist incidents on Indian soil (non-Kashmir)</td><td>27 major attacks 2005-2011. Over 1,000 civilians killed in bomb blasts in Jaipur, Ahmedabad, Delhi, Mumbai, Varanasi, Pune. Serial bombing campaigns treated as law-and-order failures rather than acts of war with state sponsors</td><td>Zero major civilian terrorist attacks on Indian soil outside Kashmir from 2014 to 2025 per government data. In Kashmir, attacks shifted from local recruitment (129 in 2019) to near-zero local recruitment (1 in 2025), indicating destruction of local political infrastructure for terrorism</td></tr><tr><td>Strategic doctrine</td><td>Strategic restraint doctrine: India absorbs attacks and responds diplomatically. Grounded in nuclear deterrence logic and desire to avoid Pakistan Army getting the conflict it wanted. Resulted in emboldened Pakistani proxy groups</td><td>Graduated deterrence doctrine: Uri surgical strikes, Balakot air strikes, Sindoor deep strikes. Each iteration escalated from the previous. Established a new implicit rule: major terrorist attacks will receive military responses of increasing scale and depth</td></tr><tr><td>Civilian terror casualties 2004-2014 vs 2014-2024</td><td>1,770 killed in terror incidents (per MHA declassified data cited by Amit Shah in Lok Sabha, July 2025)</td><td>357 killed in terror incidents (per same source). 80 percent reduction. Terrorist deaths: 123 percent increase. Security force casualties: reduced from 1,060 to 542</td></tr><tr><td>Key structural reform failures</td><td>CDS not created despite Kargil Review Committee recommending it in 2000. Military-civil friction not resolved. Jointness between services minimal. Defence production dominated by government PSUs with no private sector participation. DRDO treated as autonomous fiefdom</td><td>CDS created 2020. Integrated Theatre Commands in progress. Private sector brought into defence manufacturing. iDEX for startups. Over 500 defence items on Positive Indigenisation List. Defence production PSUs restructured into accountable DPSUs. Defence exports reach 100+ countries</td></tr></tbody></table>`
